shader: lower HMMA to one HMMA_NATIVE pseudo-instruction (backport of heydemoura 0013)

Backport of heydemoura's patch 0013 (main at ed38fcd) to Eglantine e736dfd plus
tools/eglantine-patches 0001-0040 (Vampinity ocarina-oot-shaders 095654b).

With EDEN_NX2_TENSOR set (=1), or when the caller asks for tensor lowering, each
HMMA.1688/.16816.F16 now becomes one HMMA_NATIVE pseudo-instruction (bits 0-7 D,
8-15 A, 20-27 B, 39-46 C, 47 K=16, opcode 0x5d38 << 48, guard predicate kept).
frontend/maxwell/translate/impl/hmma_native.cpp builds the same IR that the
core's Maxwell expansion translates to: the same lane shuffles, f16->f32
conversions, FFMA order and rounding to half after every eight products. It does
this without about 230 Maxwell words per HMMA.16816, the scratch registers or the
borrowed register quartet. EDEN_NX2_HMMA_NATIVE=0 keeps the core's expansion.
EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=stub (D = C) and unset (the stand-in upscale) are unchanged.

The shuffles (32) and f32 FMAs (64) per HMMA.16816 stay the same, so the host
driver's compile cost changes little. What shrinks is the lowered program and
its translation.

Differences from 0013: the core has no soft_hmma/cooperative-matrix path (0009)
and no tensor_mul_add.cpp, so the pseudo-instruction is emitted after the core's
own HMMA field checks, and the translator is self-contained. No cache version
bump: a native program's pipeline key is the hash of its lowered code
(shader_environment.cpp Analyze, shader_cache.cpp MakeShaderInfo), so the new
lowering gets new keys and stored pipelines from either lowering are never bound
by the other. A bump would only delete every game's cache file.
EDEN_NX2_IR_STATS=1 logs IR size, shuffles and FMAs for programs with 16 or more
shuffles. For native compute programs start= is always 0x50 (sizeof(sph)), and
pipelines compiled from the disk cache at boot are logged too.

